configure line and build script are in the public Credits page and GitHub Issues on Droid-Stream-Releases. For three years from each release we send
this exact source on request (open an issue on
https://github.com/1tordroid/Droid-Stream-Releases).

SMB browsing uses SMBJ (com.hierynomus:smbj) under the Apache License 2.0.
Credentials for network sources are kept in an encrypted on-device store.

Direct magnet playback and the Torrents tab use one libtorrent session
through libtorrent4j (org.libtorrent4j:libtorrent4j), both under the BSD
3-Clause License. The stream is served to the player from http://127.0.0.1
only. Seeding is off unless the user turns it on. NanoHTTPD
(org.nanohttpd:nanohttpd) serves that local stream under the BSD license.
OkHttp (com.squareup.okhttp3:okhttp), Apache License 2.0, performs the
segmented downloads.

Dolby Vision profile 7 to 8.1 conversion in the built-in player
follows the RPU layout and
conversion rules of dovi_tool's dolby_vision crate
(https://github.com/quietvoid/dovi_tool). It is a separate Kotlin
implementation; dovi_tool's test RPUs are used as test data in
automated tests. dovi_tool is under the MIT License:

